{% comment %}
  Compact horizontal product card for the cart drawer's "You may also like"
  strip.

  Deliberately NOT snippets/cartel-card.liquid:
    - that snippet is frozen (docs/lane-reports/7c-cart.md);
    - it is vertical and carries class="card", which cartel-home.css:105 pins at
      flex:0 0 296px on EVERY template — two thirds of a 440px drawer;
    - it derives its form id from section.id (:25), and `section` is nil in the
      drawer, so ids would collapse to `cartel-add--{product id}` and collide.

  No <form> and no <product-form> here, on purpose:
    - assets/product-form.js is loaded per SECTION (main-product:43,
      featured-product:510, the three grids, cartel-product-row:25,
      main-cart-items:15) and never by layout/theme.liquid, so a <product-form>
      in the always-rendered drawer would be inert on /blogs, /pages, /404 and
      the account templates;
    - a <form> anywhere under #CartDrawer-Form would be dropped by the HTML
      parser, taking product-form.js's unguarded this.form with it.
  The button is driven by the delegated handler in assets/cartel-conversion.js.

  Accepts:
    - card_product: {product} required. The caller has already excluded products
      that are in the bag, sold out, $0 "price on request" or Thuya-gated.

  Usage:
    {% render 'cartel-drawer-upsell-card', card_product: p %}
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign p = card_product
  assign v = p.selected_or_first_available_variant
-%}
<li class="uc">
  {%- comment -%}
    ONE link around image, name and price. cartel-card.liquid uses two (:30 and
    :43); here that would be 3 cards x 3 stops = 9 tab stops before Checkout.
    alt is empty on purpose — the link's accessible name is the title inside it,
    and a duplicated name is announced twice.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <a class="uc-link" href="{{ p.url }}">
    {%- if p.featured_media -%}
      {{
        p.featured_media
        | image_url: width: 160
        | image_tag: class: 'uc-photo', widths: '52,104,156', sizes: '52px', loading: 'lazy', alt: ''
      }}
    {%- else -%}
      {% render 'cartel-photo-placeholder', ph_size: 'xs', ph_class: 'uc-photo' %}
    {%- endif -%}
    <span class="uc-txt">
      <span class="uc-name">{{ p.title | escape }}</span>
      <span class="uc-price">{{ v.price | money }}</span>
    </span>
  </a>
  {%- if p.variants_count > 1 -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Multiple variants cannot be quick-added without a picker, so this one
      leaves the bag for the product page.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <a class="btn btn-out uc-add" href="{{ p.url }}">Options</a>
  {%- else -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      type="button" and no form= attribute: this sits outside #CartDrawer-Form,
      and with JS off it must do nothing rather than POST /cart and lose the bag.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <button
      type="button"
      class="btn btn-fill uc-add"
      data-uc-add="{{ v.id }}"
      data-uc-title="{{ p.title | escape }}"
      aria-label="Add {{ p.title | escape }} to your bag"
    >
      <span class="uc-add-t">+ Add</span>
      {%- render 'loading-spinner' -%}
    </button>
  {%- endif -%}
</li>
